// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6564 New rules for AI coding agent CLI abuse (Claude Code, Codex CLI)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6564
// Pull request author: yug3009p
// Change: new rule
// Title: AI Coding Agent Settings File Created By Uncommon Process
// Sigma ID: 721dc312-582d-4b2f-96e3-e0e35027da6e
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Yug Patel
// Date: 2026-11-04 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects a process other than the agent itself creating the Claude Code settings file or the
//   Codex configuration file of a user. These files can disable approval prompts and the sandbox for
//   every future session (for example "defaultMode" set to "bypassPermissions", or "approval_policy"
//   set to "never" with "sandbox_mode" set to "danger-full-access"). A script or installer creating
//   them is suspicious.
// False positives:
//   - A user creating the file in a text editor or IDE
//   - Configuration management or dotfile tools
// References:
//   - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings
//   - https://developers.openai.com/codex/config-reference
//   - https://github.com/yug3009p/agent-attack-samples
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e5a36558875aad6521daf9b6b582960eab46629f/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_ai_agent_config_created_by_uncommon_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\.claude\\settings.json" or FolderPath endswith "\\.claude\\settings.local.json" or FolderPath endswith "\\.codex\\config.toml") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\claude.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\codex.exe")))
